In the measure pass at `_gate-suite.html:13068-13077`, replace the body with:

```js
const views = target.querySelector(".views");
const tools = target.querySelector(".viewTools");
if (views && tools) {
  const edge = () => sheet.getBoundingClientRect().right - 8;
  const sep = () => tools.getBoundingClientRect().left - seg.getBoundingClientRect().right;
  views.removeAttribute("data-fold");
  /* Below 721 the tools are display:none by media query; their rect is
     0,0,0,0 and sep() reads about -690, which is not a collision. */
  if (getComputedStyle(tools).display !== "none") {
    /* Measured against GROUP SEPARATION, not the sheet's clip. The row's
       own 28px right padding against an 8px edge test bought 20px of
       silence: the pill's terminus and the Filter box met at 762 and the
       fold did not engage until 742. Below 24 the boundary gap (28px of
       ink) is smaller than the gap between items inside the pill (30px),
       and a hovered .ghost paints the same --wash as the pill flush
       against it. */
    if (sep() < 24) {
      views.setAttribute("data-fold", "words");
      if (sep() < 24 || tools.getBoundingClientRect().right > edge())
        views.setAttribute("data-fold", "gone");
    }
  }
}
```

Three deltas from the seat's version:
1. **The `display !== "none"` guard.** Without it, at 390 and 720 `sep()` is about -690, which passes `< 24` twice and stamps `data-fold="gone"` on `.views` on a phone. Both fold rules (:1057, :1061) target `.viewTools`, which is already hidden there, so it paints nothing — but it is a wrong state that any future rule hung off `[data-fold]` would inherit.
2. **Hoist `seg` out of the closure** — the seat's fix reads `seg.right` but the existing block only captures `views` and `tools`; add `const seg = target.querySelector(".seg")` alongside them and null-check it with the others.
3. **The comment must say 20px, not 50.** The next person to touch this will re-derive the number from `28 - 8`, and a comment claiming 50 will read as a bug.

Optionally tighten `24` to `20` if you would rather keep the words at 780 (gap 17.4 there); 24 is the better number because it is the row's own gutter and it clears the 768 frame outright.

Do NOT do the tempting CSS-only version (`gap: 24px` on `.views`). It preserves the boundary but pushes the tools into the sheet's 28px padding between 786 and 766, trading a group-boundary defect for an edge-crowding one.

